      "detail": "It comes straight from Astral, who make uv, and OpenAI, who make the Codex CLI, over an encrypted connection, as it would if you installed it yourself. When you press Install/Update Translation Environment, it downloads uv's install script from Astral and runs it (if you don't already have uv), then uses uv to build a Python 3.12 environment from a hash-locked package list, as its README says. For OpenAI sign-in, its install button (after a one-time notice) or update prompt likewise runs OpenAI's Codex CLI install script, which the README also says. Nothing checks either install script; on Windows they run straight from the web. We reviewed version 3.6.0; this release has the same code."
